{"id":"mahabharata-3-234","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":234,"title":"चतुस्त्रिंशदधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 234 · Arjuna and Chitrasena","summary":{"en":"The Gandharvas rain arrows from the sky, and Arjuna answers with divine weapons, hemming them in with a net of arrows. Chitrasena fights him with magic until Arjuna overpowers him, and then reveals himself as Arjuna's friend from heaven; the warriors greet one another on their chariots.","kn":"ಗಂಧರ್ವರು ಆಕಾಶದಿಂದ ಬಾಣಮಳೆಗರೆಯುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಅರ್ಜುನನು ದಿವ್ಯಾಸ್ತ್ರಗಳಿಂದ ಉತ್ತರಿಸಿ ಬಾಣಜಾಲದಲ್ಲಿ ಅವರನ್ನು ಸುತ್ತುವರಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಚಿತ್ರಸೇನನು ಮಾಯೆಯಿಂದ ಹೋರಾಡಿ ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಂದ ಸೋತಾಗ ತಾನು ಸ್ವರ್ಗದ ಮಿತ್ರನೆಂದು ತೋರಿಕೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ವೀರರು ರಥಗಳಲ್ಲೇ ಪರಸ್ಪರ ಕುಶಲ ವಿಚಾರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"गन्धर्व आकाश से बाणों की वर्षा करते हैं, और अर्जुन दिव्यास्त्रों से उत्तर देकर उन्हें बाणों के जाल में घेर लेते हैं। चित्रसेन माया से लड़ता है जब तक अर्जुन उसे परास्त नहीं कर देते, फिर स्वयं को स्वर्ग का उनका मित्र बताता है; योद्धा रथों पर ही एक-दूसरे का कुशल पूछते हैं।","te":"గంధర్వులు ఆకాశం నుండి బాణవర్షం కురిపిస్తారు, అర్జునుడు దివ్యాస్త్రాలతో బదులిచ్చి బాణజాలంలో వారిని చుట్టుముడతాడు. చిత్రసేనుడు మాయతో పోరాడి అర్జునుని చేతిలో ఓడినప్పుడు తాను స్వర్గంలోని మిత్రుడనని వెల్లడిస్తాడు; వీరులు రథాలపైనే పరస్పరం కుశలం అడుగుతారు.","ta":"கந்தர்வர்கள் வானிலிருந்து அம்பு மழை பொழிய, அர்ஜுனன் தெய்வீக அஸ்திரங்களால் பதிலளித்து அம்பு வலையில் அவர்களைச் சூழ்கிறான். சித்ரஸேனன் மாயையால் போரிட்டு அர்ஜுனனிடம் தோற்றதும் தான் ஸ்வர்க்கத்து நண்பன் என்று வெளிப்படுத்த, வீரர்கள் தேர்களிலேயே ஒருவரையொருவர் நலம் விசாரிக்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"ഗന്ധർവന്മാർ ആകാശത്തുനിന്ന് അമ്പുമഴ ചൊരിയുന്നു; അർജുനൻ ദിവ്യാസ്ത്രങ്ങളാൽ മറുപടി നൽകി അവരെ അമ്പുകളുടെ വലയിൽ തടയുന്നു. മായാവിദ്യയാൽ ചിത്രസേനൻ പോരാടുന്നു; അർജുനൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ കീഴടക്കുന്നു, പിന്നെ താൻ സ്വർഗ്ഗത്തിൽനിന്നുള്ള അർജുനന്റെ സുഹൃത്താണെന്ന് വെളിപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു; യോദ്ധാക്കൾ തേരുകളിലിരുന്ന് പരസ്പരം അഭിവാദ്യം ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.234; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"घोषयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Ghoshayatra Parva (The cattle expedition)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो दिव्यास्त्रसंपन्ना गन्धर्वा हेममालिनः ।\nविसृजन्तः शरान्दीप्तान्समन्तात्पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Gandharvas, wearing golden garlands and gifted with divine weapons, loosed blazing arrows and surrounded the Pandavas on every side."}},{"n":2,"text":"चत्वारः पाण्डवा वीरा गन्धर्वाश्च सहस्रशः ।\nरणे संन्यपतन्राजंस्तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The four Pandava heroes and the Gandharvas by the thousand fell upon each other in the battle, O king, and it was a marvel to see."}},{"n":3,"text":"यथा कर्णस्य च रथो धार्तराष्ट्रस्य चोभयोः ।\nगन्धर्वैः शतशश्छिन्नौ तथा तेषां प्रचक्रिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Just as the Gandharvas had cut to pieces by hundreds the chariots of Karna and of Dhritarashtra's son, so they tried to do to the Pandavas."}},{"n":4,"text":"तान्समापततो राजन्गन्धर्वाञ्शतशो रणे ।\nप्रत्यगृह्णन्नरव्याघ्राः शरवर्षैरनेकशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those tigers among men met the Gandharvas, hundreds of them rushing in, with many showers of arrows."}},{"n":5,"text":"अवकीर्यमाणाः खगमाः शरवर्षैः समन्ततः ।\nन शेकुः पाण्डुपुत्राणां समीपे परिवर्तितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Covered on all sides by the arrow showers, the sky-goers could not come near the sons of Pandu."}},{"n":6,"text":"अभिक्रुद्धानभिप्रेक्ष्य गन्धर्वानर्जुनस्तदा ।\nलक्षयित्वाथ दिव्यानि महास्त्राण्युपचक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna, seeing the Gandharvas enraged, took note of them and began to use his great divine weapons."}},{"n":7,"text":"सहस्राणां सहस्रं स प्राहिणोद्यमसादनम् ।\nआग्नेयेनार्जुनः संख्ये गन्धर्वाणां बलोत्कटः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, strong in battle, sent a thousand thousand of the Gandharvas to the abode of Yama with the fire weapon."}},{"n":8,"text":"तथा भीमो महेष्वासः संयुगे बलिनां वरः ।\nगन्धर्वाञ्शतशो राजञ्जघान निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too Bhima, the great archer and best of the strong, struck down the Gandharvas by hundreds with sharp arrows, O king."}},{"n":9,"text":"माद्रीपुत्रावपि तथा युध्यमानौ बलोत्कटौ ।\nपरिगृह्याग्रतो राजञ्जघ्नतुः शतशः परान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two sons of Madri, powerful fighters, also seized their foes in front of them and killed them by hundreds."}},{"n":10,"text":"ते वध्यमाना गन्धर्वा दिव्यैरस्त्रैर्महात्मभिः ।\nउत्पेतुः खमुपादाय धृतराष्ट्रसुतांस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by those great-souled men's divine weapons, the Gandharvas flew up into the sky, taking Dhritarashtra's sons with them."}},{"n":11,"text":"तानुत्पतिष्णून्बुद्ध्वा तु कुन्तीपुत्रो धनंजयः ।\nमहता शरजालेन समन्तात्पर्यवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them rising, Dhananjaya, son of Kunti, enclosed them on every side in a great net of arrows."}},{"n":12,"text":"ते बद्धाः शरजालेन शकुन्ता इव पञ्जरे ।\nववर्षुरर्जुनं क्रोधाद्गदाशक्त्यृष्टिवृष्टिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bound in that net of arrows like birds in a cage, they poured down on Arjuna in rage a rain of maces, spears and lances."}},{"n":13,"text":"गदाशक्त्यसिवृष्टीस्ता निहत्य स महास्त्रवित् ।\nगात्राणि चाहनद्भल्लैर्गन्धर्वाणां धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That master of great weapons struck down those showers of maces, spears and swords, and cut the Gandharvas' limbs with broad-headed arrows."}},{"n":14,"text":"शिरोभिः प्रपतद्भिश्च चरणैर्बाहुभिस्तथा ।\nअश्मवृष्टिरिवाभाति परेषामभवद्भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Heads, feet and arms falling looked like a rain of stones, and fear gripped the enemy."}},{"n":15,"text":"ते वध्यमाना गन्धर्वाः पाण्डवेन महात्मना ।\nभूमिष्ठमन्तरिक्षस्थाः शरवर्षैरवाकिरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by the great-souled Pandava, the Gandharvas, some on the ground and some in the air, showered him with arrows."}},{"n":16,"text":"तेषां तु शरवर्षाणि सव्यसाची परंतपः ।\nअस्त्रैः संवार्य तेजस्वी गन्धर्वान्प्रत्यविध्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Arjuna, the left-handed archer and scorcher of foes, blocked their arrow showers with his weapons and pierced the Gandharvas in return."}},{"n":17,"text":"स्थूणाकर्णेन्द्रजालं च सौरं चापि तथार्जुनः ।\nआग्नेयं चापि सौम्यं च ससर्ज कुरुनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, joy of the Kurus, let loose the weapons named Sthunakarna, the Indrajala, the solar, the fiery and the lunar."}},{"n":18,"text":"ते दह्यमाना गन्धर्वाः कुन्तीपुत्रस्य सायकैः ।\nदैतेया इव शक्रेण विषादमगमन्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Burned by the son of Kunti's arrows, the Gandharvas fell into great despair, like the Daityas before Indra."}},{"n":19,"text":"ऊर्ध्वमाक्रममाणाश्च शरजालेन वारिताः ।\nविसर्पमाणा भल्लैश्च वार्यन्ते सव्यसाचिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they tried to rise upward they were stopped by the net of arrows, and when they scattered, the left-handed archer checked them with broad-headed shafts."}},{"n":20,"text":"गन्धर्वांस्त्रासितान्दृष्ट्वा कुन्तीपुत्रेण धीमता ।\nचित्रसेनो गदां गृह्य सव्यसाचिनमाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Gandharvas terrified by the wise son of Kunti, Chitrasena took up a mace and ran at Arjuna."}},{"n":21,"text":"तस्याभिपततस्तूर्णं गदाहस्तस्य संयुगे ।\nगदां सर्वायसीं पार्थः शरैश्चिच्छेद सप्तधा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he rushed on with the mace in hand, Arjuna cut his all-iron mace into seven pieces with arrows."}},{"n":22,"text":"स गदां बहुधा दृष्ट्वा कृत्तां बाणैस्तरस्विना ।\nसंवृत्य विद्ययात्मानं योधयामास पाण्डवम् ।\nअस्त्राणि तस्य दिव्यानि योधयामास खे स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his mace cut up by the swift archer's arrows, he wrapped himself in magic and fought the Pandava, standing in the sky, using his own divine weapons."}},{"n":23,"text":"गन्धर्वराजो बलवान्माययान्तर्हितस्तदा ।\nअन्तर्हितं समालक्ष्य प्रहरन्तमथार्जुनः ।\nताडयामास खचरैर्दिव्यास्त्रप्रतिमन्त्रितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty king of the Gandharvas vanished by illusion. Noticing him striking from hiding, Arjuna struck back with weapons empowered by divine mantras and aimed at things moving in the sky."}},{"n":24,"text":"अन्तर्धानवधं चास्य चक्रे क्रुद्धोऽर्जुनस्तदा ।\nशब्दवेध्यमुपाश्रित्य बहुरूपो धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Angered, Arjuna then set about killing him while hidden, aiming by sound, assuming many forms."}},{"n":25,"text":"स वध्यमानस्तैरस्त्रैरर्जुनेन महात्मना ।\nअथास्य दर्शयामास तदात्मानं प्रियः सखा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he was being struck by those weapons of the great-souled Arjuna, his dear friend showed himself."}},{"n":26,"text":"चित्रसेनमथालक्ष्य सखायं युधि दुर्बलम् ।\nसंजहारास्त्रमथ तत्प्रसृष्टं पाण्डवर्षभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his friend Chitrasena weak in the fight, that bull of the Pandavas withdrew the weapon he had loosed."}},{"n":27,"text":"दृष्ट्वा तु पाण्डवाः सर्वे संहृतास्त्रं धनंजयम् ।\nसंजह्रुः प्रद्रुतानश्वाञ्शरवेगान्धनूंषि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Dhananjaya draw back his weapon, all the Pandavas held back their galloping horses, their arrows' speed and their bows."}},{"n":28,"text":"चित्रसेनश्च भीमश्च सव्यसाची यमावपि ।\nपृष्ट्वा कौशलमन्योन्यं रथेष्वेवावतस्थिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chitrasena, Bhima, Arjuna and the twins asked after each other's welfare and remained standing in their chariots."}}]}]}